-- #1037 (S0 silent wrongness + SIGSEGV): a decl ATTRIBUTE on an `impl` made the impl
-- VANISH.  `parseAttrib` wraps ANY decl in `DAttrib attrs <decl>`; `lowerDeclImpl`
-- (core_ir_lower) and `declImplEntries` (eval) both matched `DImpl` and fell through
-- everything else to `_ => []`, so an attributed impl contributed NO entry at all.
-- The interpreter then answered from the interface DEFAULT (wrong value, exit 0) and
-- the native binary segfaulted through #948's arm-less dispatcher.
--
-- An attribute is METADATA.  It must never change which impls exist, and this fixture
-- pins that for every axis the bug had:
--
--   Cat  @deprecated, OVERRIDES, reached through a CONSTRAINED FORWARDER (dict-routed)
--   Dog  no attribute, INHERITS — the sibling whose presence made Cat's loss silent
--   Fox  @inline, OVERRIDES, reached by a DIRECT call (the RKey path, not the chain)
--   Owl  @must_use, OVERRIDES — a THIRD attribute name: the defect was never about
--        `deprecated`, it was about the `DAttrib` wrapper
--
-- `catNoise` also pins the DCE half: an attributed impl's method body must seed
-- reachability roots (`isEmittingDecl` said False for `DAttrib`), or the helper it
-- alone calls is dropped and the emitter aborts `unbound variable 'catNoise'`.  That
-- was latent only because the impl emitted no body to dangle; making the impl exist
-- is exactly what would have armed it.
--
-- `shout` pins the sibling case: an attribute written directly on a DEFINITION (with
-- NO separate signature line) wraps the DFunDef itself, and `funGraphInto` /
-- `definedFnNamesInto` skipped it — so `shoutBody`, called only from there, was DCE'd
-- and `medaka build` died with `unbound variable 'shoutBody'` on a check-green,
-- run-correct program.  (Write the attribute above a SIGNATURE and it wraps the DSig
-- instead, leaving the DFunDef bare — which is why only this form reproduces.)
--
-- Must print:  meow / woof / fox / owl / shouted
import aface.{Speak(..), speak}

data Cat = Cat
data Dog = Dog
data Fox = Fox
data Owl = Owl

catNoise : Unit -> String
catNoise _ = "meow"

shoutBody : Unit -> String
shoutBody _ = "shouted"

@deprecated "old"
impl Speak Cat where
  speak _ = catNoise ()

-- INHERITS `speak`, alongside Cat's attributed override.
impl Speak Dog where


@inline
impl Speak Fox where
  speak _ = "fox"

@must_use
impl Speak Owl where
  speak _ = "owl"

@inline
shout = shoutBody ()

useSpeak : Speak a => a -> String
useSpeak x = speak x

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = putStrLn (useSpeak Cat)
  let _ = putStrLn (useSpeak Dog)
  let _ = putStrLn (speak Fox)
  let _ = putStrLn (useSpeak Owl)
  putStrLn shout
